  "question": {
    "text": "For <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>N</mi></math>, consider a relation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi></math> given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo></math>{<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>:</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>y</mi></math> is a multiple of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math>}. The relation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;is an equivalence relation if and only if"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn></math>",
